{"qid":"Q2288","names":["Tver"],"title":"Tver","endonym":{"native":"Тверь","lang":"ru"},"capsule":"The Grand Principality of Tver was established c. 1247 when Alexander Nevsky granted it to his brother Yaroslav Yaroslavich, and it rapidly became Moscow's chief rival for leadership of northeastern Rus. Prince Mikhail Yaroslavich (r. 1305–1318) won the patent for the grand principality of Vladimir but was executed by the Golden Horde after Moscow-backed accusations in 1318; his son Dmitry suffered the same fate in 1326. Despite later alliances with Lithuania and Tver's cultural flourishing—including Afanasy Nikitin's celebrated journey to India (1466–1472)—the principality could not withstand sustained Muscovite pressure: Ivan III besieged the city in 1485 and the last prince, Mikhail Borisovich, fled to Lithuania, ending two and a half centuries of Tver's independence.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. The principality's political history is well documented in Russian chronicles and Mongol records; its fluctuating outer boundaries vis-à-vis Novgorod, Muscovy, and Lithuania are reconstructed from treaty texts rather than surveyed frontiers.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Grand Duchy of Tver","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grand_Duchy_of_Tver"},{"label":"Britannica: Tver","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Tver"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Mikhail of Tver","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mikhail_of_Tver"}],"britannica":"place/Tver-Russia","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Tver","rulers":[{"qid":null,"name":"Yaroslav Yaroslavich","nativeName":"Ярослав Ярославич","roman":"Yaroslav Yaroslavich","start":1247,"end":1271,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Sviatoslav Yaroslavich","nativeName":"Святослав Ярославич","roman":"Sviatoslav Yaroslavich","start":1271,"end":1285,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Mikhail Yaroslavich","nativeName":"Михаил Ярославич","roman":"Mikhail Yaroslavich","start":1285,"end":1318,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Dmitry Mikhailovich (the Terrible Eyes)","nativeName":"Дмитрий Михайлович Грозные Очи","roman":"Dmitry Mikhailovich","start":1318,"end":1326,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Alexander Mikhailovich (1st reign)","nativeName":"Александр Михайлович","roman":"Alexander Mikhailovich","start":1326,"end":1327,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Konstantin Mikhailovich (1st reign)","nativeName":"Константин Михайлович","roman":"Konstantin Mikhailovich","start":1327,"end":1338,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Alexander Mikhailovich (2nd reign)","nativeName":"Александр Михайлович","roman":"Alexander Mikhailovich","start":1338,"end":1339,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Konstantin Mikhailovich (2nd reign)","nativeName":"Константин Михайлович","roman":"Konstantin Mikhailovich","start":1339,"end":1345,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Vasily Mikhailovich","nativeName":"Василий Михайлович","roman":"Vasily Mikhailovich","start":1349,"end":1368,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Mikhail Alexandrovich","nativeName":"Михаил Александрович","roman":"Mikhail Alexandrovich","start":1368,"end":1399,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Ivan Mikhailovich","nativeName":"Иван Михайлович","roman":"Ivan Mikhailovich","start":1399,"end":1425,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":nu